        431,
        814
      ],
      "margin_number": 158,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "When two things are being compared, Greek uses ἤ, 'than', e.g.\nὁ ἀνὴρ ἐστι σοφώτερος ἢ ὁ παῖς. 'The man is wiser than the boy.'\nNote that the two things being compared are in the same case.",
